message: "If you use Su-Tech, please cite it as below."
title: "Su-Tech: explainable irrigation advice from the FAO-56 water balance with a weekly soil check"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tolobek
    given-names: Osman
version: "0.9.0"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/osmanri/sutech-core"
url: "https://t.me/Su_Tech_bot"
keywords:
  - irrigation scheduling
  - FAO-56
  - water balance
  - decision support
  - Kazakhstan
abstract: >-
  Su-Tech is a Telegram bot and Mini App that gives a farmer daily irrigation advice (whether to irrigate, how many
  cubic metres, what the pump costs) from the weather at the field, using the FAO-56 root-zone water balance.
  All coefficients are checked against the FAO tables (docs/COEFFICIENT_CHECK.md). The results are from a
  computer study on real weather (model against model), not field measurements. The code was written with an AI
  assistant; the idea, the checking of formulas, the Arduino test bench and the experiment are the author's.
